<title>RUSSIA: Russia to auction 12 trln rbls T-bills March 5.</title>
<headline>Russia to auction 12 trln rbls T-bills March 5.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Finance Ministry will offer 7.50 trillion roubles of 238-day GKO discount Treasury bills and a new 4.50 trillion rouble 133-day tranche of existing T-bills at an auction on March 5, the Central Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auctions follow. </p>
<p>Details of 238-day bills</p>
<p>    Series number	 22075</p>
<p>    Issue volume	  7.50 trillion roubles</p>
<p>    Denominations	 1.00 million roubles</p>
<p>    Tenor		   238 days</p>
<p>    Issue date	    March 5</p>
<p>    Maturity date	 October 29</p>
<p>Details of 133-day bill tranche</p>
<p>    Series number	 22069 (additional tranche)</p>
<p>    Issue volume	  4.50 trillion roubles</p>
<p>    Denominations	 1.00 million roubles</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)   133 days</p>
<p>    Issue date	    March 5</p>
<p>Original issue date February 5</p>
<p>    Maturity date	 July 16</p>
<p>The series 22069 bills were the first to be subject to a new 15 percent tax on earnings from government securities.</p>
<p>The earlier tranche of the 22069 bills closed on Tuesday at 89.29, yielding 31.05 percent.</p>
<p>On March 5 the Finance Ministry will also repay 8.60 trillion roubles of maturing 210-day T-bills (series 22044).</p>
<p>--Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
